chx:Research a res:ResearchProject ; rdfs:label "Threads for an advanced course: chapter 25 as the Threads subject of the 2nd edition's multithreading material and today's Python 3.14.6 threading, executors, GIL and free-threaded build"@en ;
    sen0414:methodology "Primary source first: the chapter's named concepts from the textbook ontology built over the published chapter. Then the official documentation for the current release and the PEPs the chapter's topics touch. Every source opened and read on 2026-10-14T20:00:00; every claim taken from text actually read; every behaviour executed under Python 3.14.6." ;
    res:hasResearchScope chx:Scope ; rdfs:member chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P07, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P17, chx:P18, chx:P19, chx:P20, chx:P21, chx:P22, chx:P23, chx:P24, chx:P25, chx:P26, chx:P27, chx:P28, chx:P29, chx:P30, chx:P31, chx:P32, chx:P33, chx:P34, chx:P35, chx:P36, chx:P37, chx:P38, chx:P39, chx:P40, chx:P41, chx:P42, chx:P43, chx:P44, chx:P45, chx:P46, chx:P47, chx:P48, chx:P49, chx:P50, chx:P51, chx:P52, chx:P53, chx:P54, chx:P55, chx:P56, chx:P57, chx:P58, chx:P59, chx:P60, chx:P61, chx:P62, chx:P63, chx:P64, chx:P65, chx:P66, chx:P67, chx:P68, chx:P69, chx:P70, chx:P71, chx:P72, chx:P73, chx:P74 .
chx:Scope a res:ResearchScope ; res:hasResearchQuestion "What does the multithreading material of chapter 17 of the 2nd edition (the Thread object, start, the args and kwargs of the target, join, concurrency issues, the multithreaded XKCD downloader and the launching of programs) teach, which of its listings and statements still hold under Python 3.14.6, what do daemon threads, locks, queues, events, semaphores, concurrent.futures executors, the global interpreter lock and the free-threaded build add to it, how do threads compare with processes and asyncio, and what must an advanced course correct or add, given that the 3rd edition dropped the material?" ; res:hasTimeWindow "Current as of 2026-10-14." .
